# NitroStack Configuration
NITRO_LOG_LEVEL=info
NITROSTACK_APP_MODE=openai

# Server Transport Configuration (Optional)
# =============================================================================
# MCP_TRANSPORT_TYPE: Toggles transport mode. Values: stdio | http | dual.
# Defaults to 'stdio' in development and 'dual' in production/NODE_ENV=production.
# =============================================================================
# MCP_TRANSPORT_TYPE=stdio
# PORT=3000
# HOST=localhost
# ENABLE_CORS=true

# ── REGISTRAR — student identity and progress storage ───────────────────────
# Both optional. Unset, the app runs exactly as before: no storage, no secret,
# no network. Persistence is a capability, not a prerequisite.
#
# MENTOR_STORE: memory | sqlite. Default memory.
#   memory  progress survives the conversation and reconnecting, but NOT a
#           restart or redeploy. Zero configuration.
#   sqlite  durable, via the Node standard library (node:sqlite) — no driver and
#           no new dependency. REQUIRES Node 22.5+; NitroCloud builds on Node 20,
#           where it is unavailable and the app FALLS BACK to memory and says so
#           rather than failing to start. Check with the whoami tool.
# MENTOR_STORE=sqlite
# MENTOR_DB_PATH=mentor.db
#
# Anonymous callers are deliberately stateless — they never read or write storage,
# because every anonymous caller shares one identity and one drawer. Progress is
# only kept for an authenticated subject (context.auth.subject).
#
# Auth itself is supplied by the SDK (JWTModule / ApiKeyModule / OAuthModule); the
# instructor role is read from an "instructor" scope or a role claim. No tool is
# hard-gated, so a judge with no account can still drive the whole loop.
